description: No Cursor or agent attribution in commits or GitHub Actions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git and CI — no agent attribution

- Never add `Co-authored-by:` trailers (or similar) that reference Cursor, Cursor Agent, or other AI tooling to commits—whether authored manually or generated by scripts and workflows.
- In `.github/workflows/**` (and any CI config): do not mention Cursor/agents in step names, comments, env vars, or in commands that format commit messages (e.g. `git commit -m`, changelog, or release notes emitted by CI).

Keep commits and automation neutral and human- or project-owned only.
